Reset hog->report_map_id after the report map read completes or is cancelled.

In BlueZ 5.86, read_report_map() sets hog->report_map_id and returns early
whenever hog->report_map_id is nonzero. Neither report_map_read_cb() nor
bt_hog_detach() clears it, so a single transient ATT read failure (or
disconnect while the read is in flight) leaves the HoG instance unable to
re-read the Report Map or create its uHID input device on any subsequent
reconnect until bluetoothd is restarted.

Keep hog->report_map_id nonzero across remove_gatt_req() in
report_map_read_cb() because remove_gatt_req() invokes read_report_map() when
a successful request drains hog->gatt_op; clear it immediately afterward and
after bt_hog_detach() cancels pending GATT requests.

--- a/profiles/input/hog-lib.c
+++ b/profiles/input/hog-lib.c
@@ -1037,6 +1037,7 @@ static void report_map_read_cb(guint8 status, const guint8 *pdu, guint16 plen,
 	ssize_t vlen;
 
 	remove_gatt_req(req, status);
+	hog->report_map_id = 0;
 
 	if (status != 0) {
 		error("Report Map read failed: %s", att_ecode2str(status));
@@ -1793,6 +1794,7 @@ void bt_hog_detach(struct bt_hog *hog, bool force)
 		bt_dis_detach(hog->dis);
 
 	queue_remove_all(hog->gatt_op, cancel_gatt_req, hog, destroy_gatt_req);
+	hog->report_map_id = 0;
 	g_attrib_unref(hog->attrib);
 	hog->attrib = NULL;
 
